  "body": "In the autocomplete examples, the spec provides as examples:\r\n\r\n```\r\naddress-level2: Cambridge\r\naddress-level1: MA\r\ncountry: US\r\n```\r\n\r\nHowever, this seems incorrect, since it's missing a County level between the municipality and state. It seems that the example should instead read:\r\n\r\n```\r\naddress-level3: Cambridge\r\naddress-level2: Middlesex County\r\naddress-level1: MA\r\ncountry: US\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe previous designators (region, locality) seem easier to use, particularly when the region (County in this example) is optional in forms, but I understand the change makes the standard more faithful to the ISO interpretation.",
